# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command which
usage 1   which <name>...               say what answers each name: an alias, a shell builtin or a command

case each kind of name
target none
covers 1
$ which cd grep quit QUIT help
out 101
cd: shell builtin
grep: command
quit: alias for shutdown
QUIT: alias for shutdown
help: shell builtin
status 0
action none
$ which hexdump c exit
out 67
hexdump: alias for xxd
c: alias for resume
exit: alias for shutdown
status 0
action none
$ which nosuch
out 16
which: no nosuch
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
$ which cd nosuch echo
out 54
cd: shell builtin
which: no nosuch
echo: shell builtin
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
$ which
out 29
which: usage: which <name>...
status 1
action none
end
